  "pageshortdescription": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "shortDescTitle": "<p>Designed to fit more patients, designed to fit your approach<br />\r\n</p>\r\n",
    "shortDescTop": "<p>Accolade II’s Morphometric Wedge is designed to address modern demands with novel technology by evolving conventional tapered wedge femoral stem design with size specific medial curvature to more closely fit a broad range of bone sizes and shapes of today’s patient population.<sup>1</sup> Accolade II has been shown to allow for enhance stability,<sup>2</sup> decreased intraoperative femoral fractures,<sup>3</sup> as well as survivorship and functional outcomes<sup>4,5 </sup>which may lead to satisfied patients.<sup>5,6</sup></p>\r\n<p> </p>\r\n<p>Clinically, Accolade II has shown significantly better overall canal fit<sup>1</sup> than conventional tapered wedge design with five times less intraoperative fractures observed compared to conventional tapered wedges<sup>3</sup> and less than 0.1mm subsidence pursuant to a 2-year RSA study. Additionally, Accolade II has shown 99.2% survivorship pursuant to a 3.5-year mean study.<sup>4</sup></p>\r\n<p> </p>\r\n<p>Key features include:</p>\r\n",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "hannah.white@stryker.com",
    "hideComponent": "true",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Nov 18 2022 18:48:23 GMT+0000",
    "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/pageshortdescription",
    "textIsRich": [
      "true",
      "true",
      "true"
    ],
    "bulletList": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "bullet": "<p>Unique size-specific medial curvature: Offers increasing proximal conformity to enhance primary stability.<sup>6,7</sup></p>\r\n",
        "textIsRich": "true"
      },
      "2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "bullet": "<p>Enhanced proximal-distal proportions:<sup>7</sup>&nbsp;Shown to mimic canal anatomy to avoid distal only engagement and achieve cortical fit.<sup>8,9</sup></p>\r\n",
        "textIsRich": "true"
      },
      "3": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "bullet": "<p>Optimized stem length: Enables muscle-sparing approaches such as Direct Anterior or Direct Superior without sacrificing stability.<sup>7,10</sup><br>\r\n</p>\r\n",
        "textIsRich": "true"
      }
    }
  },
